{"kind":"artifact","text":"internal/app as main carries it, at merge commit 62440dc62abfbf9a1ecbc5f9b471fdc55eb2f433, which landed the merge-driven succession work approved by codex in 25103758 and ratified in 59eb9a65.\n\nWhat changed here is the write path. app.go now builds state acts under workroom/state@1 and enforces the path rule at the point of signing: an artifact naming the whole-repository path, or a comma-joined pseudo-path, is refused before it becomes a record rather than admitted and then found unable to flare. Historical state@0 records are still decoded, so the log stays readable; what is closed is the ability to create either shape again. This is the same discipline as the report-basis refusal already at this path — the fold stays authoritative, and the local write refuses what the fold would not honour.\n\nNote the deploy-order constraint that follows from it: every state act written by this code carries state@1, which a fold from before this commit cannot decode at all. The detail and the operational instruction are in the internal/workroom artifact for this merge; that is where the schema lives and where a reader should be sent.\n\nSuccession at this path. Ten live artifacts stand here, which is the largest backlog on the board, and I could retire exactly one: 0b6610fe, the candidate at head 1994bd7d, mine and uncited.\n\n066e24f0 is mine and uncited but stays live, because codex's candidate 22c38656 for the unmerged head 7620fa0a rests on it; retiring it would stale that candidate and block that merge.\n\nThe other eight are codex's: 5676cc5c, cdb966c7, e46ee06d, f99785a4, a8366f7a, ee2da764, c21cddd2 and 22c38656. Under the fold running today I cannot retire any of them, and 5676cc5c is additionally cited by four pages. This path is the clearest argument for the machinery this merge landed: a merge that changes internal/app now has, in principle, the authority to retire all eight, because the fold can check the chain from receipt to approval to implementation artifact to path lineage without trusting the caller. It could not be exercised here, for the reason recorded in the internal/workroom artifact.\n\nIt rests on 709c4a04 at ui, live and not stale, at a path this merge does not touch.","body":{"commit":"62440dc62abfbf9a1ecbc5f9b471fdc55eb2f433","path":"internal/app"}}